---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Helper function to create proper asset URLs
const getAssetUrl = (path: string) => {
  const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
  return base.endsWith('/') ? `${base}${path}` : `${base}/${path}`;
};
---

<Layout title="The Secret Harmony - A Fantasy Novel" description="Discover The Secret Harmony, an epic fantasy novel about Iris Evershade and her journey into a forgotten, forbidden Harmony.">
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="relative py-12 lg:py-18 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-900/90 to-emerald-900/80"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-5 mb-12 lg:mb-0">
          <div class="relative">
            <img src={getAssetUrl('images/book-cover.jpeg')} alt="The Secret Harmony Book Cover" class="w-full max-w-lg mx-auto rounded-lg shadow-2xl border border-emerald-800/30">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-emerald-900/20 to-transparent rounded-lg"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <p class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-6 font-['Cinzel']">
            The Secret Harmony
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            A fantasy novel of Harmonic Magic, forbidden knowledge, and the battle against corruption.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            In the forested world of I'lyr, all power flows through Harmony — the music that shapes the living world. Iris Evershade knows more about its theory than anyone at the Arbory of Elm, even her instructors. Year after year, the simplest melody falls apart the moment she sings it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            Then a woman she never knew dies — a great-aunt, hidden away, erased from every record — and leaves her an abandoned cottage at the edge of nowhere and a mysterious journal written in words no living person can read. What the cottage hides is an ancient secret banned for so long it has been forgotten.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            But it's not the only thing waiting for her. Her great-aunt released something that was locked away in the silence between the harmonies. It offers Iris the one thing she has wanted her whole life: to belong so completely she will never feel broken again. She has only to stop fighting and let go.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            When Iris discovers what it truly wants, she realizes she is the only person alive who can banish it again. The only acolyte in eons, trained by failures in the field — she has to become enough. And to do that, she has to stop believing the lie she has carried since she was small: that something inside her was broken beyond fixing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
            The girl who only ever asked questions must become the answer. And the one song she was never taught is the one she cannot sing alone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Characters -->
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-12 text-center font-['Cinzel']">
        Meet the Characters
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-8 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-3 font-['Cinzel']">Iris Evershade</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-lg">
            She understands the theory of Harmony better than anyone at the Arbory of Elm — and cannot sing the simplest melody without it unraveling in her hands. Iris has spent her life believing she is broken. Her almond-shaped eyes shift between green and gray, her voice carries overtones she never means to make, and she answers questions no one has spoken aloud. What her instructors read as failure is something they have forgotten how to name: the connective Harmony that once bridged every tradition, waiting in the boundaries between them for the one lyral who can hear it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-8 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-3 font-['Cinzel']">Laurel Silverbrook</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-lg">
            Iris's closest friend, with auburn hair that falls in thick waves against deep walnut skin — a coloring that once made her a target and now turns every head in a room. Warm, quick, and effortlessly disarming, Laurel names a feeling before others notice they have it. But the easy charm is a craft she honed against childhood cruelty, and beneath it lives a mind no one has been allowed to see: three years of private harmonic study locked in a chest she has shown to no one. Her loyalty to Iris is unshakable. Her own power is only beginning to surface.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-8 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-3 font-['Cinzel']">Reed Mistwater</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-lg">
            The tallest and quietest of Iris's circle, Reed carries his strength with deliberate gentleness, letting others speak first so his rare words land with weight. He learned healing at his dying grandmother's side years before he entered the Arbory, and he treats Harmony as a way to ease suffering rather than a subject to master. His knowledge of the marsh traditions and Wild Harmonies runs deeper than the formal schools allow. He pours what he feels for Iris into quiet acts — a found text, a gift left without a note — long before he finds the courage to say it aloud.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-8 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-3 font-['Cinzel']">Rowan Emberfall</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-lg">
            An Elder of the Arbory of Ash who trusts only what he can measure. After detecting an impossibility from the remote Northlands, Rowan turns his relentless analytical gaze on Iris. His voice carries the crystalline edge of Ash mastery, his praise rare and clipped. What begins as cold investigation hardens into confrontation, then bends toward an uneasy alliance, as the most rigorous mind in I'lyr confronts truths that lie beyond the reach of measurement.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-8 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-3 font-['Cinzel']">Linnea Brightwillow</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-lg">
            An Elder of the Arbory of Elm whose measured grace and layered wisdom have made her one of the most revered voices in I'lyr. Linnea believes the Harmonies were tragically fractured long ago, and that she alone carries the intellect and dedication to make them whole again. Every word she speaks works on more than one level; her warmth runs deep, and so does the pride beneath it. She would sacrifice anything to restore the order she reveres — and it is precisely her virtues that make her the most dangerous person Iris will ever face.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-8 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-3 font-['Cinzel']">Alder Nightwind</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-lg">
            A wandering herbalist with weathered clothes, an easy manner, and a talent for asking small questions that draw out large answers. Alder is none of what he appears: an independent operative hired to watch Iris, a man who surrenders information by the drop and gathers it by the flood. He prizes knowledge and his own freedom above every cause and every person — or so he insists. Neither villain nor hero, he plays each side for advantage, until the evidence of Iris's character begins to compel the one thing he has spent a lifetime avoiding: belief in something beyond himself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- World Building -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-slate-800/50">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-12 text-center font-['Cinzel']">
        The World of I'lyr
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-6 font-['Cinzel']">The Arbories</h3>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="M11 20A7 7 0 0 1 9.8 6.1C15.5 5 17 4.48 19 2c1 2 2 4.18 2 8 0 5.5-4.78 10-10 10z"/><path d="M2 21c0-3 1.85-5.36 5.08-6C9.5 14.52 12 13 13 12"/></svg>
                Elm
              </h4>
              <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Connection, flexibility, and intuition. Masters of emotional harmony and interpersonal bonds.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="m17 14 3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H4.7a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L7 14h-.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L9 9h-.2A1 1 0 0 1 8 7.3L12 3l4 4.3A1 1 0 0 1 15.2 9H15l3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H17Z"/><path d="M12 22v-3"/></svg>
                Oak
              </h4>
              <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Endurance, protection, and truth. Specialists in defensive magic and structural integrity.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="M12 22V12"/><path d="m17 7-5 5-5-5"/><path d="M12 12C12 6 7 4 4 6c3 0 5 2 8 6z"/><path d="M12 12c0-6 5-8 8-6-3 0-5 2-8 6z"/></svg>
                Birch
              </h4>
              <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Renewal, clarity, and purification. Healers and cleansers of corruption.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="M11 20A7 7 0 0 1 9.8 6.1C15.5 5 17 4.48 19 2c1 2 2 4.18 2 8 0 5.5-4.78 10-10 10z"/><path d="M2 21c0-3 1.85-5.36 5.08-6C9.5 14.52 12 13 13 12"/></svg>
                Ash
              </h4>
              <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Sacrifice, transformation, and wisdom. Masters of change and deep understanding.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="m17 14 3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H4.7a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L7 14h-.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L9 9h-.2A1 1 0 0 1 8 7.3L12 3l4 4.3A1 1 0 0 1 15.2 9H15l3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H17Z"/><path d="M12 22v-3"/></svg>
                Fir
              </h4>
              <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Resilience, focus, and aspiration. Specialists in persistence and goal achievement.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-6 font-['Cinzel']">Key Settlements</h3>
          <div class="space-y-6">
              <div class="space-y-4">
                <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
                  <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"/></svg>
                    Underfen
                  </h4>
                  <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Ancient marsh settlement with pre-Ebony origins and the mysterious Seven Hollows.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
                  <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="m17 14 3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H4.7a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L7 14h-.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L9 9h-.2A1 1 0 0 1 8 7.3L12 3l4 4.3A1 1 0 0 1 15.2 9H15l3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H17Z"/><path d="M12 22v-3"/></svg>
                    Thornbriar
                  </h4>
                  <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Protective forest community suspicious of Arbory influence.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
                  <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"/></svg>
                    Willowmere
                  </h4>
                  <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">A vibrant market town near the Elm Arbory where diverse cultures mingle freely, home to the Silverbrook family.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
                  <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20"/><path d="M2 12h20"/></svg>
                    Millhaven
                  </h4>
                  <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">A fiercely independent town of three centuries, west of the Fir Arbory, with its own harmonic traditions untouched by the Arbory system.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
                  <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="shrink-0"><path d="M2 12s3-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3 7-10 7-10-7-10-7Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg>
                    Resonance
                  </h4>
                  <p class="text-slate-300 text-md">Perfectly preserved research center from pre-fragmentation era.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Geography of I'lyr -->
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-12 text-center font-['Cinzel']">
        Geography of I'lyr
      </h2>
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
        <!-- Map Display -->
        <div class="relative group">
          <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-lg border-2 border-emerald-800/30 hover:border-emerald-600/50 transition-colors duration-300 bg-slate-900/30 p-4">
            <a href={getAssetUrl('images/ilyr-prime.jpg')} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="block">
              <img
                src={getAssetUrl('images/ilyr-prime.jpg')}
                alt="Detailed map of I'lyr showing the Five Arbories, settlements, and geographic features"
                class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg shadow-2xl cursor-pointer transition-transform duration-300 hover:scale-105"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </a>
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-900/40 to-transparent pointer-events-none rounded-lg"></div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-center text-sm text-slate-400 mt-4 italic">
            Click to view larger version • <a href={getAssetUrl('images/ilyr-prime.jpg')} download="ilyr-prime-map.jpg" class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300">Download Map</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Map Information -->
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-6 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-4 font-['Cinzel']">The Realm of I'lyr</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-300 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
              I'lyr spans a vast expanse of primeval forests, ancient marshlands, and towering mountains. At its heart stand the Five Arbories, each representing a different harmonic tradition and serving as centers of learning and power.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-300 text-lg leading-relaxed">
              Beyond the Arbories, numerous settlements—from the marsh-dwelling communities to isolated forest villages—maintain their own traditions, some predating the formal Arbory system itself.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-slate-900/50 p-6 rounded-lg border border-emerald-800/30">
            <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold text-emerald-300 mb-3 font-['Cinzel']">Geographic Features</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300 text-lg">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="m17 14 3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H4.7a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L7 14h-.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7-1.7L9 9h-.2A1 1 0 0 1 8 7.3L12 3l4 4.3A1 1 0 0 1 15.2 9H15l3 3.3a1 1 0 0 1-.7 1.7H17Z"/><path d="M12 22v-3"/></svg>
                <span><strong>The Great Forest:</strong> Dense primeval woodland covering most of I'lyr</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="M12 22a8 8 0 0 1-8-8c0-4.314 6-12 8-12s8 7.686 8 12a8 8 0 0 1-8 8z"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Southern Marshlands:</strong> Ancient wetlands home to guardian spirits of the reeds</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="m8 3 4 8 5-5 5 15H2L8 3z"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Mountain Ranges:</strong> Natural barriers defining regional boundaries</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-1"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Abandoned Settlements:</strong> Mysterious ruins holding forgotten knowledge</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-emerald-900/20 p-6 rounded-lg border border-emerald-600/30">
            <p class="text-emerald-300 text-lg">
              <strong>Explore Further:</strong> Each location on this map plays a role in Iris's journey. Some harbor ancient secrets, others represent political power, and a few hold the key to understanding the Corrupted Whisper itself.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Call to Action -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-900/50 to-slate-900/50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-6 font-['Cinzel']">
        Ready to Enter I'lyr?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 mb-8">
        Join Iris Evershade on her journey of discovery, friendship, and the courage to challenge everything she's been taught.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="/stories" class="border border-emerald-600 text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-600 hover:text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold transition-colors duration-200">
          Read Short Stories First
        </a>
        <a href="/about" class="bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold transition-colors duration-200">
          Meet the Author
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>